26:["$","aside",null,{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/25 bg-amber-500/5 p-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground","role":"note","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-medium text-foreground","children":"Educational only — not investment advice"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","children":"ContentVerse India publishes general financial education. Nothing here is a buy/sell recommendation, portfolio advice, or a substitute for a SEBI-registered adviser. Markets involve risk; verify figures with your broker, bank, or official filings."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-xs","children":"Last reviewed: September 2026. Confirm live rules on official portals."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-xs","children":["Useful official sources",":"," ",[["$","span","https://www.sebi.gov.in/",{"children":[null,["$","$L8",null,{"href":"https://www.sebi.gov.in/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"text-primary hover:underline","children":"SEBI"}]]}],["$","span","https://www.rbi.org.in/",{"children":[" · ",["$","$L8",null,{"href":"https://www.rbi.org.in/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"text-primary hover:underline","children":"RBI"}]]}],["$","span","https://www.nseindia.com/",{"children":[" · ",["$","$L8",null,{"href":"https://www.nseindia.com/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"text-primary hover:underline","children":"NSE"}]]}]]]}]]}]
27:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-8 xl:flex-row xl:items-start","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-0 flex-1 space-y-10","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl space-y-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl font-semibold","children":["How to use ","SIP Calculator"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"A SIP (Systematic Investment Plan) lets you invest a fixed amount in a mutual fund every month instead of putting in a lump sum. This SIP calculator estimates how much your monthly investment could grow to over time at an assumed annual return. It shows the amount you invested, the estimated gain and the projected maturity value — useful for goal planning such as a child’s education, a house down payment or retirement."}]]}],[["$","div","How to use the SIP calculator",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"How to use the SIP calculator"}],[["$","p","Enter the monthly amount you plan to invest, the",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Enter the monthly amount you plan to invest, the annual return you expect and the number of years. The calculator compounds the return every month and treats each instalment as invested at the start of the month, which matches how most SIPs work."}],["$","p","The expected return is an assumption, not a prom",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"The expected return is an assumption, not a promise. Equity mutual funds have delivered double-digit returns over some long periods and negative returns over others. Try three scenarios — a cautious one (for example 8%), a moderate one (10–12%) and an optimistic one — and plan around the cautious case."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Monthly investment: the amount debited from your bank every month",{"children":"Monthly investment: the amount debited from your bank every month"}],["$","li","Expected annual return: your assumed long-term growth rate (not guaranteed)",{"children":"Expected annual return: your assumed long-term growth rate (not guaranteed)"}],["$","li","Time period: SIPs work best over 7–10 years or more because compounding needs time",{"children":"Time period: SIPs work best over 7–10 years or more because compounding needs time"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex justify-center py-2","children":["$","aside",null,{"aria-label":"Advertisement","data-cv-ad-zone":"mrec","className":"mx-auto flex w-fit max-w-full flex-col items-center","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1.5 text-center text-[9px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted-foreground/70","children":"Ad"}],["$","$L2c",null,{"slotKey":"inArticle","width":300,"height":250}]]}]}]]}],["$","div","How SIP returns are calculated",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"How SIP returns are calculated"}],[["$","p","The future value of a SIP is FV = P × [((1 + i)^",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"The future value of a SIP is FV = P × [((1 + i)^n − 1) ÷ i] × (1 + i), where P is the monthly instalment, i is the monthly rate (annual rate ÷ 12 ÷ 100) and n is the number of months. Each instalment earns returns for a different length of time, which is why early instalments matter more than late ones."}],"$L2d"],null,null]}],"$L2e","$L2f"]]}],"$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34"]}],"$L35"]}]
