2d:["$","p","Real mutual funds do not grow in a straight line",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Real mutual funds do not grow in a straight line. Returns come as changing NAVs, and exit loads, expense ratios and taxes reduce what you finally take home. This calculator shows a smooth projection so you can compare plans, not predict your exact balance."}]
2e:["$","div","Why starting early beats investing more later",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"Why starting early beats investing more later"}],[["$","p","Because returns compound, time in the market is ",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Because returns compound, time in the market is often more powerful than the monthly amount. Investing ₹5,000 a month for 20 years at an assumed 12% builds a corpus close to ₹50 lakh from ₹12 lakh invested. Investing the same ₹5,000 for only 10 years gives about ₹11.6 lakh from ₹6 lakh. Doubling the time does far more than doubling the contribution."}],["$","p","If you cannot raise your SIP today, consider a s",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"If you cannot raise your SIP today, consider a step-up: increase the monthly amount by 5–10% each year as your income grows. Even a small yearly increase noticeably changes the final corpus."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Match the investment to the goal horizon: equity for 7+ years, debt or hybrid for shorter goals",{"children":"Match the investment to the goal horizon: equity for 7+ years, debt or hybrid for shorter goals"}],["$","li","Review the plan once a year instead of reacting to market news every week",{"children":"Review the plan once a year instead of reacting to market news every week"}],["$","li","Check the fund’s expense ratio, category and risk level before you start",{"children":"Check the fund’s expense ratio, category and risk level before you start"}]]}],null]}]
2f:["$","div","What this calculator does not include",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"What this calculator does not include"}],[["$","p","It does not subtract capital-gains tax, exit loa",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"It does not subtract capital-gains tax, exit load or fund expenses, and it does not adjust for inflation. A corpus of ₹50 lakh in 20 years will buy less than ₹50 lakh does today. When you set a goal, inflate the target cost first and then work backwards to the SIP amount."}]],null,null]}]
